      "question": "If $\\dfrac{a}{b}$ is rational ($b\\neq0$), prove that its additive inverse is $-\\dfrac{a}{b}$.",
      "answer": "Additive inverse of $\\dfrac{a}{b}$ is $-\\dfrac{a}{b}$ because $\\dfrac{a}{b}+\\left(-\\dfrac{a}{b}\\right)=\\dfrac{0}{b}=0$.",
      "options": [],
      "glassboxSteps": [
